Hmm — idempotent signature: `idempotent(requestId, hash, type, action, fallback)`. The fallback is used when DuplicateKeyException occurs and no request record found. For create → SUBSTATION_EXISTS. For updateCap → could duplicate come from anything? updateCap doesn't insert unique rows except request record... audit insert has no unique constraint. So duplicate only from request record → replay path handles. Fallback for updateCap: REQUEST_ID race where record exists → replay handles; if not found → shouldn't happen; fallback conflict("REQUEST_CONFLICT"...). I'll give a generic fallback per call.

